WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:16.090
Despite being a small country with barely
20 million inhabitants, for at least the last

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:25.280
seven decades, Taiwan has been a hot spot
of international politics.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:28.860
Its official name is not Taiwan, but the "Republic
of China".

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:33.720
This is because its origin goes back to the
country that emerged in China after the Xinhai

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:34.720
Revolution of 1912.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:39.200
A revolution that led to the fall of the Qing
Dynasty.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:42.740
However, the story doesn't end there.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:47.539
A few years later, China was to face a new
nightmare with the invasion of the Japanese

00:01:47.539 --> 00:01:52.440
Empire, which managed to control the richest
and most powerful parts of the new country,

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:57.550
and whose capitulation in 1945 served as a
breeding ground for the outbreak of a new

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:03.580
power struggle: that of Mao's communists against
the republicans of the Kuomintang nationalists.

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:11.700
And so, you can imagine who won, right?

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:17.620
Mao was able to establish his people's republic
in mainland China, while the leaders of the

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:23.890
counter-revolution and what remained of their
army settled on the island of Formosa.

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:30.310
There, they created a state considered for
decades to be the legitimate successor of

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:35.010
the model government that existed in Mainland
China prior to the invasion of Japan and the

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:36.350
subsequent communist revolution.

00:02:36.350 --> 00:02:40.670
That one thing is important, the legitimate
government of the Republic of China.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:44.560
And in this way, for more than 30 years the
nationalist government of Taiwan was, for

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:47.870
many countries, the valid interlocutor, the
Government of China.

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:50.430
The natural successor of the Xinhai Revolution.

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:52.690
The legitimate government of the entire country.

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:58.070
Viewed from this perspective, Mao's regime
was nothing more than a government that illegitimately

00:02:58.070 --> 00:02:59.790
occupied mainland China.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:06.790
In fact, that has traditionally been the claim
of the Taiwanese authorities.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:11.330
And we need to tread carefully here, because
we are not exactly talking about a democracy,

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:16.070
but of a rigid dictatorship under the control
of Chiang Kai Sek.

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:19.550
To give you an idea, there were no elections
held there until 1996.

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:24.520
In spite of this and thanks to its alliance
with the United States, until 1971, the Republic

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:25.690
of China, i.e.

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:31.220
Taiwan, occupied the seat that belongs to
China at the United Nations to the detriment

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:35.380
of the People's Republic founded and controlled
by Mao Zedong.

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:40.500
In 1971, however, everything began to change.

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:48.480
That year Taiwan lost its seat at the UN in
favour of the People's Republic of China.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:51.810
Of course, let’s see, a country can only
have one representative in the UN.

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:56.040
And if there are two governments that consider
themselves to be legitimate, then… you have

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.850
to choose one or the other.

00:03:57.850 --> 00:04:02.800
And therein lies the problem, Taiwan has never
been considered as an independent country,

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:05.390
but as the legitimate China.

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:07.989
What a mess!

00:04:07.989 --> 00:04:14.459
From that moment on, international recognition
and the global influence of Taiwan have done

00:04:14.459 --> 00:04:16.400
nothing but plummet.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:21.440
Now, what happened to the Taiwan that was
once fully recognized by all the major western

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:22.440
powers?

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:25.430
What will become of it now that mainland China
has become a superpower?

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:27.620
What happened to Taiwan’s claims?

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:31.710
And what is even more important, what can
we expect after the enormous protests that

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:36.310
have occurred in Hong Kong, and the recent
presidential elections of January 2020 in

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:37.310
Taiwan?

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:44.500
Let’s take a look!

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:54.330
(FROM LEGITIMATE HEIR TO POLITICAL NUISANCE)

00:04:54.330 --> 00:05:00.610
As I’ve just explained, for many years the
government of Taiwan was, for most countries,

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:04.250
the sovereign representative of the Chinese
nation.

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:09.360
Of course, the increasing influence of the
People's Republic of China together with the

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:16.810
economic awakening of the Asian giant, has
really turned the tables.

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:21.510
Taiwan began losing recognition from all the
countries with a few exceptions from smaller

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:22.680
nations.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:28.030
The United States, Taiwan’s most important
ally, officially switched its recognition

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:32.270
to the People's Republic of China to the detriment
of the Republic of China under the Carter

00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:39.279
Administration in 1979.

00:05:39.279 --> 00:06:01.110
Currently, only 14 countries in addition to
the Vatican recognize the Republic of China

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:07.200
as the valid state of China.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:12.500
This situation and the fact that even the
fiercest allies of Taiwan cease to officially

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:17.380
recognize them, led the island government
to abandon its claim as legitimate government

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:23.409
of China in the early 1990s.

00:06:23.409 --> 00:06:28.029
Since then, Taiwan has relaxed its efforts
on recognition and has opted for a strategy

00:06:28.029 --> 00:06:33.020
that is becoming increasingly clear and is
gaining more support over time: Not to be

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:37.669
recognized as the Republic of China, but only
as Taiwan.

00:06:37.669 --> 00:06:41.270
Given the story so far, that makes perfect
sense.

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:45.870
The Taiwanese understand all too well that
the political, social, economic and democratic

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:51.000
measures they have taken over the years on
the island have created a great divide between

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:53.050
it and mainland China.

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:58.589
The lifestyle, current politics and society
in Taiwan are completely different to what

00:06:58.589 --> 00:07:02.930
exists in the People's Republic of China under
the Communist Party dictatorship.

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:06.969
There are increasing differences in Taiwanese
society and the island's government already

00:07:06.969 --> 00:07:11.640
understands how insurmountable these are,
and doesn’t view the possibility of melding

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:13.930
with mainland China worth the struggle.

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:16.880
Purely and simply, Taiwan is a foreign country.

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:21.220
(AUDIO: “China’s suppression of Taiwan
in the international arena cannot change the

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:26.140
indisputable fact of Taiwan’s existence,
nor can it coerce the Taiwanese people into

00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:31.410
abandoning their democratic and free way of
life,” - Taiwan’s Ministry of Foreign

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:32.410
Affairs)

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:36.620
We could say that those who only a couple
of generations ago founded a country of exiled

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:42.500
people on an island have managed to create
an independent nation with its own idiosyncrasies.

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:48.260
And that is precisely the idea defended by
the current President Tsai Ing Wen, of the

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:50.219
Democratic Progressive Party.

00:07:50.219 --> 00:07:53.890
But, wait a moment, there is one more important
thing to point out.

00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:57.270
This particular vision is not shared by all.

00:07:57.270 --> 00:08:04.649
The Kuomintang, another major party in Taiwan
defends a very different position: to build

00:08:04.649 --> 00:08:07.810
closer ties and come to an understanding with
the Chinese regime.

00:08:07.810 --> 00:08:08.810
But...

00:08:08.810 --> 00:08:09.810
Wait a moment, did I say Kuomintang?

00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:13.659
Does that name ring any bells?

00:08:13.659 --> 00:08:20.080
Exactly, the Kuomintang is the party founded
by the nationalist republican leaders who

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:24.710
fought against the Chinese communist revolution
and established the present Taiwan.

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:26.130
Yes, that’s right.

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:30.320
Even though it sounds incredible, the party
that once went head to head with the Chinese

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:32.890
regime now advocates to be their friend.

00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:36.190
Then, there are those that say nothing ever
changes in politics.

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:37.229
Ha!

00:08:37.229 --> 00:08:40.468
In this case the switches are more frequent
than an Instagrammer snapping selfies.

00:08:40.468 --> 00:08:41.979
Now, the question that crops up is…

00:08:41.979 --> 00:08:44.560
What on earth has led to such a turnaround?

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:48.080
Well, money plays a crucial role in every
aspect of this story.

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:49.080
Yes, yes, the money.

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:52.770
And I am not just referring to bribes, kickbacks
or opaque agreements of all kinds, but to

00:08:52.770 --> 00:09:01.180
the possibility of taking advantage of the
huge economy that has been developed in mainland

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:05.320
China.

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:10.330
And it is precisely here where we hit a crucial
question: Which would you choose?

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:14.780
Fight for the full independence of your country,
although it means risking economic relations

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:18.510
with an Asian superpower or seek an understanding
with Beijing?

00:09:18.510 --> 00:09:21.330
That is not an easy question by any means.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:25.649
This is the big question the Taiwanese are
trying to answer and their collective answer

00:09:25.649 --> 00:09:29.240
will determine the electoral result.

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:34.560
Now, before we go on, there is a question
we haven’t covered.

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:39.180
What’s been happening with Taiwan since
it began losing international recognition?

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:40.240
Has it been isolated?

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:41.630
The short answer is…

00:09:41.630 --> 00:09:42.630
No.

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:46.900
Taiwan is an exception, it is not officially
considered a country, but there is a de facto

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:50.090
international recognition regarding its sovereignty
and self-government.

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:57.780
Their former international embassies have
become "economic and cultural offices", which

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:00.080
act as embassies, de facto as well.

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:04.160
The Taiwanese have identity documents and
passports issued by their own government that

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:06.860
are internationally recognized.

00:10:06.860 --> 00:10:10.410
And, this is something that angers Beijing.

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:15.050
Few things bother the government of the People's
Republic of China as much as seeing how Taiwan

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:17.820
is, in practice, an independent country.

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:21.990
(AUDIO: Taiwan must and will be reunited with
China.

00:10:21.990 --> 00:10:25.740
Independence will only bring hardship and
the re-unification with the mainland was an

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:29.680
inevitable requirement for the great rejuvenation
of the Chinese people.”

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:30.680
Xi Jinping)

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:33.280
But do not think for a second that they put
up with this.

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:34.280
No.

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:38.180
The Chinese Government, the government of
Xi Jinping, has been harassing the island

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:41.860
for years with strategies designed to wear
them down.

00:10:41.860 --> 00:10:43.130
How exactly?

00:10:43.130 --> 00:10:47.190
Many of you can imagine, I’m sure.

00:10:47.190 --> 00:10:52.740
China’s pockets are deep, extremely deep;
and don’t make the mistake of thinking there

00:10:52.740 --> 00:10:57.580
are only a couple of countries willing to
cast Taiwan aside in exchange for a handful

00:10:57.580 --> 00:10:58.580
of investments.

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:00.850
We all know too well that money talks.

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:07.960
But, just a moment, all this does not mean
that Taiwan is alone in the world.

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:10.580
That’s something that China hasn’t managed
to achieve.

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:13.770
Another thing that, by the way, drives them
crazy as well.

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:19.680
You see, even if it is only recognized diplomatically
by a handful of governments, the Taiwanese

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:24.240
retain many allies and common interests with
a lot of countries.

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:28.830
In particular there’s an agreement with
the US that has been in place since the end

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:33.560
of the 70s which states that the great American
power ensures that the island will be stocked

00:11:33.560 --> 00:11:34.840
with military equipment.

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:38.620
(AUDIO: “Changes in the diplomatic arena
are indeed challenging.

00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:43.030
But Taiwan still has many friends around the
world willing to stand with us, and we are

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:44.030
not alone.”

00:11:44.030 --> 00:11:46.460
- Tsai Ing Wen, president of Taiwan.)

00:11:46.460 --> 00:11:50.200
So, as we’ve already discussed in a previous
video that I’ll leave a link for in the

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:54.460
description, the Taiwanese government has
opted for the strategy of differentiation:

00:11:54.460 --> 00:12:00.060
We have nothing to do with China, we are Taiwan
and we do not intend to rule over anyone other

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:02.950
than ourselves, nor allow anyone to rule over
us.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:12.470
This is the message from President Tsai that
has struck a deep chord with Taiwanese voters.

00:12:12.470 --> 00:12:16.181
In the recent presidential elections, the
victory of Tsai has been overwhelming: she

00:12:16.181 --> 00:12:21.440
got 58% of the votes, a difference of almost
20 points over the Kuomintang party of Han

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:24.040
Kuo Yu.

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:28.280
So this is much more than a simple victory.

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:32.130
What Tsai has done electorally is to take
a steamroller, throw the candidates in the

00:12:32.130 --> 00:12:34.610
asphalt and roll right over the top of them.

00:12:34.610 --> 00:12:41.430
But why is it that the Taiwanese have voted
in this way despite the constant warnings

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:46.290
of Beijing against the new government of Tsai
Ing Wen?

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:50.810
Listen up!

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:58.130
(TAIWAN: THERMOMETER OF CHINESE EXPANSIONISM)

00:12:58.130 --> 00:13:03.760
The recent elections of January 2020 in Taiwan
have been a tremendous democratic slap in

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:08.710
the face to the Beijing regime.

00:13:08.710 --> 00:13:12.760
With the lessons learned from the recent events
in Hong Kong, the Taiwanese have seen the

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:16.680
eyes of the beast clearer than ever.

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:22.900
The constant meddling by Beijing in hongkongese
affairs, the violation of the special status

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:27.779
of the city, and the huge protests to claim
back freedom, have led the Taiwanese to lose

00:13:27.779 --> 00:13:31.020
the very little trust they had left in China.

00:13:31.020 --> 00:13:37.860
That is why they have voted against the Kuomintang
and its trust in Beijing.

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:43.921
A trust which, they claim, would result in
economic stability - That is to say, Chinese

00:13:43.921 --> 00:13:48.870
money and peace in the region, or put another
way, a reduction in the influence of the United

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:51.580
States.

00:13:51.580 --> 00:13:57.090
However, the opinion of the Taiwanese people
has been very different.

00:13:57.090 --> 00:14:02.180
The nearly 20 points difference achieved by
Tsai Ing Wen marks the greatest electoral

00:14:02.180 --> 00:14:05.230
victory since elections have been held in
the country.

00:14:05.230 --> 00:14:09.680
(AUDIO: “The results of this election carry
an added significance.

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:14.440
They have shown that when our sovereignty
is threatened, the Taiwanese people will shout

00:14:14.440 --> 00:14:17.840
our determination even more loudly back.”

00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:19.890
Tsai Ing Wen, president of Taiwan)

00:14:19.890 --> 00:14:24.750
Tsai has been able to take advantage of the
fear the Taiwanese have about loss of freedom

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:29.410
due to the influence of China, and it’s
a point she drove home in her final campaign

00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:30.410
speech.

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:31.410
Listen:

00:14:31.410 --> 00:14:34.990
(AUDIO; “The young people of Hong Kong have
used their lives, as well as their blood and

00:14:34.990 --> 00:14:39.630
tears, to demonstrate to us that ‘one country,
two systems’ is unworkable.

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:44.750
Tomorrow, let our young people of Taiwan demonstrate
to them that the values of democracy and freedom

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:47.250
will overcome all difficulties.”

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:49.420
- Tsai Ing Wen, president of Taiwan.)

00:14:49.420 --> 00:14:54.070
The difficulties that Tsai is talking about
are international political isolation and

00:14:54.070 --> 00:14:58.810
loss of investments.

00:14:58.810 --> 00:15:03.800
The Asian giant is hell-bent on isolating
Taipei in order to stifle its economy and

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:08.150
force the island nation to surrender to their
demands if they want to maintain their standard

00:15:08.150 --> 00:15:09.150
of living.

00:15:09.150 --> 00:15:15.570
And to this end they are not hesitating to
flash some cash.

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:20.370
We have seen it most recently with two of
the few countries that still recognized Taiwan

00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:24.410
as the legitimate government of China: the
Solomon Islands and Kiribati.

00:15:24.410 --> 00:15:29.370
(AUDIO: China extends influence in Pacific
as Solomon Islands break with Taiwan - The

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:30.370
Guardian)

00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:35.540
(AUDIO: Taiwan loses another ally as Kiribati
cuts ties - BBC)

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:40.000
Two small territories in the Pacific that
could have been key for the United States

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:43.160
in the containment of Chinese expansionist
aspirations.

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:47.780
But now the balance seems tilted more than
ever toward Beijing.

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:55.220
Of the fourteen countries that still recognize
Taiwan, there are only four in the South Pacific

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:56.220
area.

00:15:56.220 --> 00:16:00.210
And the recognition or not of Taiwan by these
countries implicitly represents their level

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:03.180
of loyalty to the United States against China.

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:06.740
Which leaves us very striking results.

00:16:06.740 --> 00:16:12.950
The lax approach of the United States in this
part of the world coupled with the giant deterring

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:17.990
power of Chinese money, have ensured that
no wars nor military ships were needed to

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:22.770
ensure control of these seas which are very
important for world trade.

00:16:22.770 --> 00:16:26.270
But… let’s not stray from the issue.

00:16:26.270 --> 00:16:31.050
The thing is that now, with another four years
of the independentist Tsai ruling Taiwan,

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:35.670
it is expected that relations with Beijing
will become colder than an ice cream in the

00:16:35.670 --> 00:16:36.670
middle of the North Pole.

00:16:36.670 --> 00:16:41.610
And when we talk about diplomatic relations
and China… we’re often talking about economic

00:16:41.610 --> 00:16:42.610
blockades.

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:46.540
That is the challenge that President Tsai
is facing…

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:51.770
Because, if there’s one thing Beijing has
argued for both actively and passively, it’s

00:16:51.770 --> 00:16:55.700
that they will never tolerate the full independence
of Taiwan.

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:59.800
(AUDIO; “We reject the ‘one country, two
systems model.

00:16:59.800 --> 00:17:03.649
We value the lifestyle of democracy, and we
defend our sovereignty.”

00:17:03.649 --> 00:17:04.649
Tsai Ing Wen)

00:17:04.649 --> 00:17:08.220
But, at this point, it’s your turn, if you
were Taiwanese, which would you choose, your

00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:11.371
political and social freedoms, or China and
the business?

00:17:11.371 --> 00:17:15.650
Do you think that Taiwan can continue growing
and developing leaving the Chinese superpower

00:17:15.650 --> 00:17:16.650
aside?

00:17:16.650 --> 00:17:18.160
Leave your answer in the comments.

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:22.510
So I really hope you enjoyed this video, please
hit like if you did, and don’t forget to

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:23.809
subscribe for brand new videos.

